{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794949628,"nonce":"kKTCCSLV6jF0QsDXGiuvBUoloao=","title":"Spec: 95b2e66 (Grow page rework)","message":"Leaflog wears the grower's Home Assistant theme. The app reads the parent HA\nfrontend's theme CSS variables (the ingress iframe is sandboxed but\nsame-origin today), converts them in pure core functions to daisyUI's oklch\nsemantic variables, applies them at the app root, and re-applies live via an\nobserver on the parent root. The main set maps: primary/accent, the three\nbackgrounds plus card and divider, primary text, and the\nsuccess/warning/error/info state colours. Fallback to the built-in theme is\nsilent and mandatory whenever the parent is unreadable or variables are\nmissing (standalone, dev, future sandbox tightening); dark and light follow\nimplicitly — no toggle. The theme harness page (a harness that iframes the\napp and sets HA-like variables on its parent root) drives the e2e. Fragility\nis logged in the decisions doc; re-check the HA developer docs at\nimplementation per AGENTS.md.\n\n\n- [ ] Core colour-conversion unit tests pin hex/rgb → oklch mapping and malformed-input fallback\n- [ ] With a harness parent setting HA-like variables, the app adopts them (asserted in rendered DOM)\n- [ ] Changing the parent's variables mid-session re-applies without reload\n- [ ] Without a readable parent, the built-in theme renders unchanged — no error UI\n- [ ] Dark and light parents both map correctly (backgrounds/text swap implicitly)\n- [ ] No Leaflog-side theme picker or toggle exists\n- [ ] Decisions-doc entries logged for the mechanism and its fragility; HA docs re-check noted\n\n\nNone (can start immediately).","files":null}]}